  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I've heard that overwriting PlayerMods once it's set is currently not possible, so maybe there could be a way to modify a world's PlayerMods through triggers locally?\n\nApplication possibilities would be: Timed speed potions, Items that grant you the jump ability or a higher jump once you obtain them, surfaces that prevent you from jumping and slow you down once you step on them, etc. This would allow more creative features to be done for worlds.\n\nThis is assuming it's not possible already in-game.",
